{
  "requirement": "Every call constructs a fresh `ValidationContext` identifying the source node\nand calls `Criterion::execute` with that context. Its completed answer, including\na negative assessment, and captured dependencies form the returned `Fingerprinted`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.inputs`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.validate_node`. I did not need to request implementation source.\n\n**Fresh `ValidationContext` that identifies the source node**\n- `concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces` runs three concurrent `verify` calls on nodes 1, 2 and 3. Each stored record holds only its own node's dependencies: `Dependency::Node(*node, …)` and `OutgoingEdges(*node, 1, …)`. The test also asserts that all three started nodes are recorded. This shows each call builds its own context for its own source node, with no shared or leaked trace.\n- `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` runs two concurrent agent verifications, \"alpha\" and \"beta\". It asserts each record's dependencies exactly: alpha has only `Node(1)`, and beta has `OutgoingEdges` plus `Node(2)`. Neither trace picks up the other's dependencies.\n- `historical_freshness_reads_do_not_enter_the_replacement_trace` calls `check_inputs`, which reads node 2, and then calls `verify`. The replacement record contains only `Node(1, \"root\")`, so earlier observations do not carry into a new call's context.\n- `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` shows the same thing: after earlier checks, the new record holds only the new execution's `Node(2)` dependency.\n\n**Calls `Criterion::execute` with that context**\n- Every test drives `verify` or `verify_with_agent`, which runs the criterion's `execute`.\n- `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts the execution counters.\n- The edge test (`agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`) has a criterion that branches on `ctx.node_id()` and records edge dependencies through the context it was given.\n\n**Completed answer, including a negative assessment, forms the returned `Fingerprinted`**\n- `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` asserts `!value.output().result` for a negative result. `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts `value.output() == &negative`. Both also check the source node, criterion path and version.\n- `review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk` checks a negative determination through the SDK path.\n\n**Captured dependencies form the `Fingerprinted`**\n- `value.dependencies()` is checked as empty in `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`.\n- `changing_one_criteria_input_does_not_invalidate_another` asserts the exact `Dependency::Node` content on the returned value.\n- The concurrent and agent tests assert the exact node and edge dependencies.\n- `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` confirms a non-`Sync` answer is returned intact.\n\nThe obligations on the `Fingerprinted` accessors are the cited `evidence.inputs` requirement's own. They are exercised here and need no further test.\n\nI found no marking gap and no untested obligation.",
